Yet another nifty class idea: the Magician. 

Note that by this I don't mean Wizard. I don't mean a magic-user at
all, in fact. I mean a good, old, razzle-dazzle, abracadabra,
sleight-of-hand stage magician. The Magician would be expert at doing
things like finding and escaping from traps (only one turn required, a
la Houndini), getting away quickly from tough fights, etc.

Class: Magician

Alignment: Neutral or Chaotic

Races: Human, elf

Starting stats: 

Extremely high charisma and dexterity. 
High intelligence.
Moderate wisdom and constitution. 
Extremely low strength. 

Intrinics: 
- speed (XL 4)
- searching (XL6)
- instant escape from all traps (XL10)
- intrinsic teleport (XL16) (so the Magician can just...vanish if
he/she gets into trouble.)

Restricted in "heavy" weapons (long sword, hammer, two-handed sword,
two-weapon combat, etc.) Unrestricted with light and ranged weaponry.
Restricted in all spell classes except escape (for getting away
quickly) and enchantment (goes with high charisma). (This restriction
is intended to stop the Magician and Wizard classes from overlapping
too much.)

Starting inventory:

A +2 baton (those little fake "wands" magicians carry. Equivalent to a
"lighter" quarterstaff for game purposes.)

One of either: cloak of displacement, cloak of invisibility, boots of
speed, or gauntlets of dexterity, enchanted to +2.

A +0 top hat (useless as armour, but when a)pplied acts as a bag of
tricks - i.e. "pulling a rabbit out of a hat.")

1 random ring drawn from the following: teleportation, teleport
control, steath, invisibility (unless you got the cloak already).

4 random objects drawn from the following: scroll of confuse monster
(since magicians are *really* good at confusing people), scroll of
light, scroll of taming, potion of confusion, potion of hallucination,
potion of invisibility, potion of levitation, potion of speed, wand of
light, wand of opening, wand of locking, wand of make invisible, wand
of secret door detection, wand of teleport.

Silk scarf (blindfold).

50% chance of a crystal ball, magic whistle, magic harp, or magic
flute.

Quest Leader: Houndini

Quest artifact: The Magic Bag (artifact bag of holding). When carried
it confers magic resistance and acts as a normal bag of holding. When
#invoked it acts as a limited wand of wishing (with major
restrictions): you are asked what you want to wish for, and "the bag
opens to reveal a <foo>." Restrictions: objects must fit inside a
standard bag, be randomly generated, and weapons/armor/tools must be
non-magical. You cannot wish for artifacts, multiple items, enchanted
weapons/armor, or wands of wishing or polymorph. In addition, the
greater the value of the item (in zorkmids), the longer the invocation
timeout.

